WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.240
A ball is thrown straight up.

2
00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:08.500
In our classroom model, its height is h
equals fifteen t minus five t squared.

3
00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:11.280
Height in metres, time in seconds.

4
00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:13.720
A dashed line marks ten metres.

5
00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:14.650
Freeze!

6
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.410
The ball is rising through
the ten metre line.

7
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.380
So when exactly is it ten metres up?

8
00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.360
Could that happen more than once?

9
00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.600
In this mission, you'll
make one side equal nought:

10
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:30.120
five t squared minus fifteen
t plus ten equals nought.

11
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:34.190
You'll factorise, then use the
rule: if A times B is nought,

12
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.300
then A or B is nought.

13
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:40.690
And you'll see each root on a graph,
where the curve crosses the x-axis.

14
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.010
Your mission: find when
the ball is ten metres up,

15
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:45.240
and explain why.
